Why dual license?

LinkMarks is a local-first bookmark manager whose optional sync relay
is network-exposed. AGPLv3 clause 13 (network use is distribution)
closes the SaaS-vector loophole: anyone who serves a modified
LinkMarks over the network must release their modifications under
AGPLv3+.

The commercial license exists for cases where a third party needs
proprietary deployment (e.g., embedded in a closed product, run as
a hosted service with custom terms). Reach out before forking for
those purposes.

